<title>BRAZIL: Embraer delivers eighth jet to U.S. firm.</title>
<headline>Embraer delivers eighth jet to U.S. firm.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian aircraft manufacturer Embraer said it has delivered the eighth jet of 25 EMB-145 jets ordered by Continental Express, a subsidiary of U.S. Continental Airlines Inc.</p>
<p>Embraer said in a statement it plans to conclude the delivery of the jets by the second quarter of 1998.</p>
<p>In September last year, Embraer signed a $375 million contract to supply Continental Express with 25 EMB-145 aircraft, with options for another 175 jets over the next 12 years, it said.</p>
<p>Embraer said Continental Express has been using its EMB-145 since early April in domestic routes.</p>
<p>((--Fatima Cristina, Sao Paulo newsroom 5511 2485412))</p>
